WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.420
A boy's schedule, in
the back of an old book:

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:08.350
"Study needed inventions"
and "Be better to parents".

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.550
Years later, a mansion's
windows blaze across a bay.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.910
And a small boat rows hard against
a current that carries it backwards.

5
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.270
A poor boy grows rich.

6
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.240
So does the novel believe
in the American Dream,

7
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.840
or bury it?

8
00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.050
In this mission, you'll find that the
phrase never appears in the novel.

9
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.850
It was popularised in 1931.

10
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:36.590
You'll study young Gatz's schedule, and
Gatsby's wish to turn back five years.

11
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.040
And you'll end where the
novel ends: "So we beat on,

12
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:44.490
boats against the current, borne
back ceaselessly into the past."

13
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.180
Your mission: decide whether
the novel believes in the dream,

14
00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:49.250
or buries it.
